Spec: SpecDD Structure Validator

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Validate SpecDD text structure against known section and line rules.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDStructureValidator.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDStructureValidator.kt

Can read:
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/parser/*
  ./SpecDDKnownSections.kt
  ./SpecDDValidationResult.kt
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/validation/SpecDDStructureValidatorBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Use the shared `@SpecDDLineClassifier` line classification boundary.
  Pass the current section label into shared line classification.
  Return validation issues sorted by start offset.
  Ignore empty text.
  Allow blank lines and comments before the first section.
  Report nonblank non-comment text before the first section as invalid syntax.
  Validate line-by-line for LF, CR, and CRLF line endings.
  Report unknown section candidates when a non-body line starts with a section-like label followed by `:`.
  Do not limit unknown section detection to uppercase labels.
  Include likely typo suggestions from `@SpecDDKnownSections`.
  Report missing `:` when a text line exactly matches a known section label.
  Report whitespace before `:` in known section header candidates.
  Require the first known section in a file to be `Spec`.
  Report a structure issue when the first known section is not `Spec`.
  Require section headers to start at column 0.
  Report leading indentation on section headers as an error.
  Ignore comment-line indentation during indentation validation.
  Require non-comment indentation to use ASCII spaces only.
  Require nonblank indentation length to be a multiple of 2.
  Report tabs, other non-space whitespace, or non-multiple-of-2 indentation as errors.
  Require body entries under a current section to use exactly 2 spaces of indentation.
  Report unindented body entries under a current section as errors.
  Treat lines indented by at least 4 spaces as continuation lines, not body entries.
  Require scenario step body entries to use exactly 2 spaces of indentation.
  Treat 4-space-or-deeper scenario-step-looking lines as continuation lines when they follow a body entry.
  Allow inline section values only for `Spec`, `Platform`, `Scenario`, and `Example`.
  Require inline section values to be separated from `:` by at least one space when content is present.
  Require `Spec` to have a nonempty inline value.
  Require `Platform` to have a nonempty inline value.
  Require `Scenario` to have a nonempty inline value.
  Allow `Example` to have an optional inline value.
  Report inline text after `:` for other known sections.
  Treat `Spec` as a bodyless section.
  Treat `Platform` as a bodyless section.
  Report follow-up text lines under `Spec` as errors.
  Report follow-up text lines under `Platform` as errors.
  Report task, scenario-step, and key-value follow-up lines under `Platform` as errors.
  Require body lines to belong to a current section that allows that body-line kind.
  Treat task-looking lines outside `Tasks` as ordinary text when the containing section accepts text.
  Validate task marker states only inside `Tasks`.
  Require task entries in `Tasks` to use exactly 2 spaces of indentation.
  Require task markers to be followed by a literal space before task text or task id when more text follows the marker.
  Require task ids to be followed by a literal space before task text when more text follows the task id.
  Require task entries in `Tasks` to contain nonempty task text after the marker and optional numeric task id.
  Report marker-only task entries as errors.
  Report task-id-only task entries as errors.
  Accept continuation lines only when a preceding body entry exists in the current section.
  Report continuation lines without a preceding body entry in the current section as invalid syntax.
  Allow continuation lines after task entries in `Tasks`.
  Report nonblank lines that are not comments, valid section headers, or valid body lines as invalid syntax.
  Allow repeated `Scenario` sections only when their inline values are different.
  Allow repeated `Example` sections.
  Report duplicate `Scenario` inline values on the second and later matching `Scenario` section.
  Report duplicate known sections other than `Scenario` and `Example`.
  Report invalid task marker states as errors.
  Report malformed task markers in `Tasks` as errors.
  Report `[invalid]` and unsupported short task states such as `[z]` as invalid task states.
  Cover valid snippets, continuation lines, exact body entry indentation, task entry indentation, task separator validation, scenario step indentation, missing task text, task-id-only entries, comment indentation, task-looking text outside `Tasks`, required scenario titles, optional example titles, unknown sections, typo suggestions, missing colons, whitespace before section colons, unsupported inline text, unsupported body lines, duplicate sections, indentation errors, section indentation, invalid task states, malformed task markers, first-section structure, line endings, empty text, comment-only text, and text before the first section in tests.

Must not:
  Define known section labels directly.
  Define parser classification behavior directly.
  Create IntelliJ annotations.
  Define highlighting colors.
  Add user-facing settings.
